==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|setja}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*satjaną}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈsɛːtja/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|ɛːtja}}
* {{a|colloquial}} {{IPA|is|/ˈsɛːta/}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-weak|setti|sett}}

# {{lb|is|transitive|governs the accusative}} to [[put]], to [[place]] something somewhere
#: {{ux|is|Nennirðu að '''setja''' forritunarbókina mína á borðið?|Could you '''put''' my programming book on the table?}}
# {{lb|is|ditransitive|governs the accusative, dative}} to [[fix]] (something for somebody), to [[determine]] (something regarding somebody), to [[decide]] (something for somebody)
#: {{ux|is|Hann '''setti''' sér það markmið að grennast.|He was '''determined''' to lose weight.}}
#: {{ux|is|Við '''settum''' okkur að leysa öll dæmin fyrir prófið.|We '''decided''' to solve all the problems before the examination.}}
# {{lb|is|transitive|governs the accusative|formal}} to formally [[open]]
#: ''Að [[setja fund|'''setja''' fund]].''
#:: To '''open''' a meeting.
# {{lb|is|ditransitive|governs the accusative, dative}} (for someone) to [[suppose]] (something)
# {{lb|is|transitive|governs the accusative}} to [[typeset]]
# {{lb|is|impersonal}} used in set phrases
#: ''Eigum við ekki að [[sjá hvað setur|sjá hvað '''setur''']]?''
#:: How about we see what happens?
#: ''Mig [[setja hljóðan|'''setti''' hljóða]] eftir símtalið.''
#:: I couldn't speak after the phone call.
#: ''Það [[setja að|sótti að mér]] kulda.''
#:: I felt cold.
#: ''Þegar hann minntist látinnar konu sinnar [[setja að grát|'''setti''' að]] honum ákafan [[setja að grát|grát]].''
#:: He began crying immensely upon remembering his deceased wife.

