==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
{{root|non|ine-pro|*sed-}}
Causative of {{m|non|sitja}}. From {{inh|non|gmq-pro|ᛊᚨᛏᛁᛞᛟ||I placed}} (''1st singular past indicative''), {{inh|non|gem-pro|*satjaną}}, from {{inh|non|ine-pro|*sodéyeti}}.

===Verb===
{{non-verb}}

# {{lb|non|transitive}} to {{l|en|seat}}, {{l|en|set}}, {{l|en|place}}, {{l|en|put}}
# {{lb|non|transitive|with accusative}} to {{l|en|drive}}
#: {{ux|non|hann setti øxina í hǫfuð honum|he drove the axe into his (not his own) skull}}
# {{lb|non|transitive|with accusative}} to {{l|en|make}}, {{l|en|establish}}
#: {{ux|non|Þeir vildu setja grið í milli konungs ok bonda|they wanted to make peace between the king and the peasants}}
# {{lb|non|transitive|with dative}} to {{l|en|order}}, {{l|en|prescribe}}
# {{lb|non|transitive|with dative}} to {{l|en|settle}}
# {{lb|non|intransitive}} to {{l|en|set off}}

